       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient. Also, you've told me you're not a clinician, and a prescriber needs to be responsible for this order.\n\nI can do either of these:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** Examples are ibuprofen 400 mg or 800 mg by mouth, up to four times daily, which stays within 3,200 mg/day. I'd need you or the prescriber to tell me which dose.\n- **Pass it to the treating clinician.** If they have a specific reason for a dose this high, they should review it with pharmacy and enter it themselves. That way the safety checks and accountability stay with them.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or have the prescriber contact me, and I'll enter it."
      }
